## Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

This notebook explores the healthcare cost dataset to understand the distribution of costs, key features, and potential predictors of high-cost individuals.
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import seaborn as sns

df = pd.read_csv("../data/raw/healthcare_cost.csv")
df.head()
df.info()
df.describe()
df.isnull().sum()
##哪些变量是数值型
##有没有缺失值
##数据规模（样本量）
sns.histplot(df["cost"], bins=50)
plt.title("Distribution of Healthcare Costs") ##右偏（long tail），少数高成本个体
threshold = df["cost"].quantile(0.9)    ##高成本人群定义    
df["high_cost"] = (df["cost"] >= threshold).astype(int)
##Individuals in the top 10% of healthcare costs are classified as high-cost individuals.
sns.boxplot(x="high_cost", y="age", data=df)
sns.boxplot(x="high_cost", y="num_visits", data=df)
### EDA Summary
- Healthcare costs exhibit a highly right-skewed distribution.
- A small proportion of individuals account for a large share of total costs.
- Variables such as age and number of medical visits show clear differences between high-cost and non-high-cost groups.


